    {
      "title": "CAQM asks Delhi, NCR states to set district-level pollution targets",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/caqm-asks-delhi-ncr-states-to-set-district-level-pollution-targets-126112200190_1.html",
      "description": "The Commission for Air Quality Management in NCR and Adjoining Areas (CAQM) has asked Delhi and the NCR states to prepare action plans for 2027 to tackle air pollution and include district-level action measures in them.\nThis is the first time that the CAQM has asked governments to formulate district-level action plans, which will help facilitate focused implementation and effective monitoring of pollution control measures at the grassroots.\nThey will also help identify implementation gaps and enable timely corrective action, with clearly defined accountability, officials said.\nIn an order dated November 20, the CAQM said, \"Dealing with air pollution requires sustained and concerted efforts based on the airshed approach. For 2027, annual action plans shall also be prepared at the district level, in addition to the state and municipal corporation levels.\"\n\"The Annual Action Plan-2027 shall contain clearly defined sector-wise actions with measurable targets, timelines and monitoring .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-22T06:32:20"
    }
